    "problem": "Previous versions of the CRU TS climate dataset lacked traceability between gridded values and input observations, and the interpolation process did not provide sufficient metadata for users to assess how data quality varies geographically.",
    "method": "This paper describes the construction of a high-resolution gridded climate dataset by interpolating monthly climate anomalies from weather station observations using angular-distance weighting (ADW) to improve traceability and allow for better diagnostics of dataset quality.",
    "task": "The task is to construct a new version of the CRU TS monthly high-resolution gridded multivariate climate dataset by interpolating weather station observations using an updated angular-distance weighting method.",
